From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:23:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fail with an error code when die is called

Since commit e5db5aa ("Check the error code of sshfs"), ERR starts as 0
and die keeps it, because ${ERR:-1} only replaces an empty value. The
EXIT trap ends with exit "$ERR", so every die after the trap is set
exits with 0, and a caller can't see the failure. A rescue system that
ran schnapps rollback on a read-only card got "Can't make snapshot of
current state" with exit code 0 and went on as if it had rolled back.

Set ERR to 1 in die unless it already holds an error code.

Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
---
 schnapps.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/schnapps.sh b/schnapps.sh
index 3831c2b..31cc32d 100755
--- a/schnapps.sh
+++ b/schnapps.sh
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ VERSION="@VERSION@"
 
 die() {
     echo "$@" >&2
-    ERR="${ERR:-1}"
+    [ "$ERR" != 0 ] || ERR=1
     exit 1
 }
 
